      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing OCR Provider**\n\nI'm currently focused on selecting an appropriate external provider for receipt OCR and information extraction, for the new Python file I'm building. The key is to find one that's easily identifiable within the code. I'm considering several options that are commonly used in the field.\n\n\n**Selecting Google Cloud Vision**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Vision AI. The `google-cloud-vision` library will be the foundation. My next step involves constructing the `extract_receipt_fields.py` file. I'm focusing on defining the `extract_receipt_fields` function, which will handle image input, Vision AI client instantiation, and text extraction using `document_text_detection`. I will simplify the text parsing, for now.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Steps**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specifics for the Python code. I plan to handle authentication through environment variables, avoiding explicit credential loading. The function I'm building, `extract_receipt_fields`, will ingest the image, instantiate the Vision AI client, and utilize `document_text_detection` for text extraction. Though the current extraction logic will be basic, the structure is designed for expansion. I'm prioritizing the integration of Google Cloud Vision AI, focusing on where I'll put placeholders for the more complex parsing. I will refine the plan for content.\n\n\n**Defining File Structure**\n\nI'm now outlining the structure of the `extract_receipt_fields.py` file, keeping Google Cloud Vision AI integration as the core. I'll import necessary libraries, define the core function, and insert comments marking where parsing logic for fields like merchant, tax, and total would reside. This plan keeps the code focused on its goal.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865787210,
          "start": 1789865781791
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
